 "verdict": "Size by Kelly weight, not flat, but at 1/8 Kelly with a 1% per-bet cap and a 10% daily exposure cap. Summed full-Kelly stakes are about 3x the bankroll on a median day, so the daily cap, not the Kelly multiplier, sets the risk; at equal exposure Kelly weighting beats flat (stake-weighted ROI +7.5% vs +4.2%). The calibrated edges are overstated (totals about 2x, spread about 1.35x), same-day outcomes are more correlated than independent bets (variance ratio 1.15-1.4), and with no true edge every scheme loses, so full and half Kelly are rejected."
}